course: dictionary
lesson: 1641
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. Context, the words around them, tells you which meaning is right. Chile with a capital C is a country. A chile with a small c is a hot pepper.
explain: «The Atacama Desert in Chile is the driest non-polar desert.» Deserts are in places, and Chile is a place, so here it must be a country. Test it: put the word country in the sentence and read it again. It still makes sense.
explain: «Mum adds one green chile to the stew, and the whole pot tastes spicy.» Stew does not have a country in it, and spicy is a clue about food. So a chile here is a hot pepper. Always ask: which meaning fits these words best?
fact: Chile is a long, narrow country in South America, between the Andes mountains and the Pacific Ocean.
fact: A chile, also spelled chili or chilli, is a small pepper that tastes hot.
fact: Chile is always a name, so it starts with a capital letter. A chile is a common word, so it usually starts with a small letter.
fact: «Chiles» is the plural, so more than one pepper is chiles.
fact: Context clues include the words before and after, capital letters, and the subject of the sentence.
exercise: «Humboldt penguins live on the coasts of Peru and Chile.» Chile sits beside Peru, so what must it be? | A pepper | A coast | A penguin | *A country
exercise: Mum says, «Add one green chile to the stew for a little heat.» What is a chile here? | A mountain range | A type of frog | *A small hot pepper | A long, narrow country
exercise: «The Atacama Desert in Chile is the driest non-polar desert.» What clue tells you Chile is a place? | The word non-polar | The word is | The word driest, which means very hot | *The word Desert, and the word in, which show where it is
test: «Red chiles can make a curry very hot.» What does chiles mean here? | Deserts | Penguins | *Peppers | Countries
test: «Chile has deserts in the north and ice in the south.» What is Chile in this sentence? | A kind of soup | *A country | A mountain | A spicy pepper
exam: «About 500 years ago the Inca ruled a huge empire along the Andes mountains, from today's Ecuador to Chile.» What is Chile in this sentence? | A river | A hot pepper | A type of empire | *A country
